nd the story it tells  starts on September 9th of 1925 late in  the afternoon and what I thought I'd do  is I'd read you just a tiny little bit  of what's happened at that moment by  5:30 the late summer Sun was already  starting to sink toward the row of  tightly packed houses the light that had  been filtering through the drawn  curtains began to fade but the gathering  darkness did nothing to dissipate the  heat that had built up over the course  of the day with the windows barely  cracked open and the door shut fast the  bungalow on the corner was enveloped in  a suffocating stillness dr. ocean suite  sat at the card table he'd set up in the  dining room he was a handsome man short  dark and powerfully built a month short  of 30 he looked 10 years older his  hairline was receding his waistline was  expanding his face was taking on the  roundness of middle-age other men might  have hated to see their youth slipping  from them sweet cultivated the illusion  of maturity where he came from black men  were permanently boys never worthy of  white men's respect never their equals  dr. sweet was no boy he was a  professional man better educated  wealthier more accomplished than most of  the whites he encountered he wanted  others to know at the moment they saw  him so he favored tailored suits well  cut and subdued he bought crisp white  shirts and tasteful ties he wore the  round tortoiseshell glasses popular with  college men he kept his mustache neatly  trimmed  his hair is stylish Lee short sweet  attempted to project the casual  confidence the instinctual authority  that set factors apart from the ordinary  run of men it didn't come to him  naturally as a child he'd shared in the  back-breaking work of his parents  Central Florida farm tending the fields  his father rented hauling water from the  stream so that his mother could do the  laundry caring for the ever-growing  brood of brothers and sisters who filled  every cranny of the tiny farmhouse his  parents had 